    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0600",
      "reading_order": 918,
      "section": "High temperature rise/low water flow systems",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 90.5697,
        "t": 270.7814000000001,
        "r": 536.8814999999993,
        "b": 245.5848000000001
      },
      "content": "For this type of application, a high water temperature rise in the energy recovery system is obtained, which consequently brings on a low flow rate.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_917",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_5",
          "title": "5       Energy recovery (optional)"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_917",
          "title": "High temperature rise/low water flow systems"
        }
      ],
      "page": 87,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0601",
      "reading_order": 919,
      "section": "High temperature rise/low water flow systems",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 90.5697,
        "t": 239.7614000000001,
        "r": 561.6072999999999,
        "b": 214.5648000000001
      },
      "content": "Example: An open circuit where cold water from a main supply is heated by the energy recovery system for use in a factory, e.g. pre-heating of boiler feed water.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_917",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
